      "type": "引用",
      "type_label": "引用",
      "text": "That’s how it happened",
      "quote": {
        "author": "firesidealpha",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2066254089756061697/MGnZGljz_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-16 09:13:32",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-16T01:13:32.000Z",
        "id": "2122135949094350967",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2122135677462880256/img/kXRuUwK4fHqOxTfA.jpg"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "duration": 46.112,
            "height": 1080,
            "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2122135677462880256/img/kXRuUwK4fHqOxTfA.jpg",
            "type": "video",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2122135677462880256/vid/avc1/1920x1080/TSs_DWeN4X9csXQq.mp4?tag=29",
            "width": 1920
          }
        ],
        "name": "Fireside Alpha",
        "text": "Elon Musk reveals he recruited SpaceX’s first engineers by telling them 'we’re probably going to die', and ended up as chief engineer because no good one would join\n\n“So SpaceX, I started that in mid-2002 expecting to fail. Probably 90% chance of failing.”\n\n“And even when recruiting people, I didn’t try to make out that it would work. I said, we’re probably going to die, but there’s a small chance we might not die, and this is the only way to get people to Mars and advance the state of the art.”\n\n“And then I ended up being chief engineer of the rocket, not because I wanted to, but because I couldn’t hire anyone who was good. None of the good chief engineers would join, because they’re like, this is too risky, you’re going to die. And so I ended up being chief engineer of the rocket.”",
        "url": "https://x.com/firesidealpha/status/2122135949094350967",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
