      "text": "Starlink helps rural schools with education",
      "quote": {
        "author": "cb_doge",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1498070100393754625/C2V-fbll_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-15 21:17:51",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-15T13:17:51.000Z",
        "id": "2121955840370614708",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2121955796431032320/img/A07_A9kkr1ta7KY5.jpg"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "duration": 10.133,
            "height": 720,
            "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2121955796431032320/img/A07_A9kkr1ta7KY5.jpg",
            "type": "video",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2121955796431032320/vid/avc1/720x720/tW2wcWiuNgn-spYw.mp4?tag=29",
            "width": 720
          }
        ],
        "name": "DogeDesigner",
        "text": "BREAKING: Every rural municipal school in Rondonópolis, Brazil, now has Starlink internet. 🇧🇷\n\nStudents and teachers can now access digital libraries, educational videos and online learning tools.\n\nSpaceX is bringing a world of knowledge to remote classrooms. ♥️",
        "url": "https://x.com/cb_doge/status/2121955840370614708",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": null,
      "reply_to": "",
      "engagement": {
        "bookmarks": 75,
        "likes": 3196,
        "quotes": 33,
        "replies": 405,
        "retweets": 320,
        "views": 499379
      },
      "url": "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2122127527040712704",
      "images": [],
      "media": [],
      "enriched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2122127355502071854",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-11-16T00:39:23.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-16 08:39:23",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "Samsung will invest $1.9 billion to expand its chip plant in Austin, Texas, to produce semiconductors for @SpaceX's Starlink satellites.\n\nThe factory is expected to produce STM32V8 chips used in Starlink's laser communication systems, shifting production currently based in France to the U.S.\n\nThe chips use an advanced 18nm FD-SOI process designed for high performance, low power consumption, and durability in harsh space environments.\n\nProduction is targeted to begin by 2030, according to the Seoul Economic Daily.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "SawyerMerritt",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1837744842715082752/xH9vYixL_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-16 07:55:23",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-15T23:55:23.000Z",
        "id": "2122116284628320705",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HXNFO3FWYAA0pPl.jpg?name=small"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "height": 720,
            "type": "photo",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HXNFO3FWYAA0pPl.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 1280
          }
        ],
        "name": "Sawyer Merritt",
        "text": "Samsung will invest $1.9 billion to expand its chip plant in Austin, Texas, to produce semiconductors for @SpaceX's Starlink satellites.\n\nThe factory is expected to produce STM32V8 chips used in Starlink's laser communication systems, shifting production currently based in France to the U.S.\n\nThe chips use an advanced 18nm FD-SOI process designed for high performance, low power consumption, and durability in harsh space environments.\n\nProduction is targeted to begin by 2030, according to the Seoul Economic Daily.",
        "url": "https://x.com/SawyerMerritt/status/2122116284628320705",
        "verified": true,
