            "width": 1080
          }
        ],
        "name": "DogeDesigner",
        "text": "BREAKING: Greece’s government is using Starlink to support a railway safety system that warns of potential train collisions. \n\nStarlink sends live train data to the control center, including through mountainous areas without mobile coverage.\n\n• Monitoring equipment installed on 134 locomotives.\n• GNSS-HEPOS positioning pinpoints trains with accuracy of up to 5 centimeters.\n• Location updates every second.\n• A 24/7 control center receives automatic collision-risk alerts so operators can intervene.",
