        "media": [
          {
            "duration": 51.916,
            "height": 1080,
            "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2121998961959636992/img/4Ulx2_gAx40ouoYb.jpg",
            "type": "video",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2121998961959636992/vid/avc1/1920x1080/rmQRJ3aLJQyzZ9X3.mp4?tag=29",
            "width": 1920
          }
        ],
        "name": "X Freeze",
        "text": "Starlink is now pulling travelers away from competing airlines\n\nUnited Airlines CEO Scott Kirby:\n\n“We already see customers moving from other airlines today”\n\nThe numbers:\n\n• Starlink is now available on more than 50% of United's daily flights\n• Over 700 aircraft equipped with Starlink\n• Full fleet rollout expected by the end of 2027\n• United's status-match campaign attracted about 4× the normal number of applications\n• 25% of those applicants already have or have applied for a United credit card\n\nKirby calls Starlink “a really unique RASM tailwind” for the airline\n\nInflight Wi-Fi used to be something travelers complained about\n\nNow it's becoming a reason to switch airlines entirely\n\nStarlink is changing the economics of airline competition",
        "url": "https://x.com/XFreeze/status/2121999050627301617",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
