      "text": "BREAKING: Samsung reportedly plans to make chips for SpaceX’s Starlink satellites in Austin, Texas. \n\nSamsung is investing $1.9 billion to expand its Austin chip factory, with the planned operations targeted to begin by 2030, according to Seoul Economic Daily.\n\nThe chip, called STM32V8, is already used in Starlink’s mini laser system. SpaceX’s Starlink engineering team has praised the chip’s performance.\n\nThe chips are currently manufactured in France. The reported Texas plan would add American production capacity for a key component behind Starlink’s satellite communications.",
